// `slotted:damage` and `slotted:max_damage` have to appear in some item's
// component map for the freeze to intern them; the item renderer reads them
// off a stack's patch to draw the durability bar.
//
// The one item in the demo data drawn from a glTF rather than from a
// primitive, so the shipped examples exercise `IconDef::Model`. The shape
// fields beside `model:` are the stand-in: they are what the CPU bake draws
// where there is no renderer and no glTF loader, and they are also what
// decides the view angle and the cell fill the model itself is rendered at.
// They describe the same pickaxe, so the two readings agree.
(
    name: "minecraft:iron_pickaxe",
    display_name: Some("Iron Pickaxe"),
    max_stack_size: 1,
    rarity: "common",
    tags: ["c:tools"],
    components: {
        "slotted:damage": 0,
        "slotted:max_damage": 250,
    },
    icon: Some((
        model: "models/pickaxe.gltf",
        shape: "rod",
        color: "#6b4c33",
        accent: "#d0d6dd",
        metallic: 0.6,
        roughness: 0.4,
    )),
)
